WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.270 --> 00:00:03.749
Hi, my name is Luv Aggarwal and I'm a data solution engineer at IBM.

00:00:04.350 --> 00:00:05.820
Ask any entrepreneur.

00:00:05.910 --> 00:00:07.980
It's way too easy to drown in data.

00:00:08.430 --> 00:00:13.199
Yes, your business generates and collects valuable information that can give you an edge over the competition.

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:17.169
But wading through the data deluge, making sense of it all,

00:00:17.169 --> 00:00:18.641
takes time and money,

00:00:18.641 --> 00:00:21.585
and often comes with security risks and delays.

00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:27.043
Part of the problem is that your data might be spread across multiple repositories and even duplicated,

00:00:27.043 --> 00:00:30.000
forcing you to normalize it all in a patchwork fashion.

00:00:30.270 --> 00:00:34.308
What's needed is a straightforward way of efficiently sorting through the glut,

00:00:34.308 --> 00:00:36.833
a process that results in faster querying,

00:00:36.833 --> 00:00:39.457
elastic scaling and real time analytics

00:00:39.457 --> 00:00:41.713
that can inform decisions immediately.

00:00:42.090 --> 00:00:46.688
And that's where Netezza Performance Server built on Cloud Pak for Data System comes into play.

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:51.261
Netezza Performance Server incorporates the market leading data warehouse

00:00:51.261 --> 00:00:54.899
and in-database capabilities of IBM PureData Systems

00:00:54.899 --> 00:00:58.474
with innovative software, hardware and architecture enhancements

00:00:58.474 --> 00:01:01.470
to deliver scalable analytics and AI solutions

00:01:01.470 --> 00:01:03.948
that exceed modern business requirements.

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:08.253
In essence, it's a high performance cloud native data warehouse

00:01:08.253 --> 00:01:11.018
with massive parallel processing capabilities

00:01:11.018 --> 00:01:14.677
that's optimized to fully leverage its Netezza DNA.

00:01:15.150 --> 00:01:17.191
It has three main hardware components:

00:01:17.322 --> 00:01:20.595
a control plane, worker enclosures and storage.

00:01:20.970 --> 00:01:22.266
As its name implies,

00:01:22.266 --> 00:01:26.430
the control plane is a group of nodes assigned a control role in the system.

00:01:26.910 --> 00:01:29.081
If we zoom in on that control plane,

00:01:29.081 --> 00:01:32.625
we see the hosts running the Netezza software and utilities.

00:01:32.880 --> 00:01:37.698
The host functions as the brain controlling and coordinating all system activity.

00:01:38.126 --> 00:01:44.149
Zoom in even closer, and we can see one of Netezza Performance Server's main attributes: simplicity.

00:01:44.690 --> 00:01:47.810
It's as easy as load-and-go with minimal administration.

00:01:48.170 --> 00:01:50.355
That means no indexing or tuning

00:01:50.355 --> 00:01:54.423
and avoiding outages for maintenance to ensure your data is always on.

00:01:55.290 --> 00:01:58.314
But while the duties of performance server is simple to use,

00:01:58.314 --> 00:02:00.311
its capabilities are sophisticated.

00:02:00.630 --> 00:02:04.598
Its reliable and mature database engine has built-in machine learning,

00:02:04.598 --> 00:02:07.843
analytics and advanced workload management capabilities,

00:02:07.843 --> 00:02:12.848
which were all developed to run complex queries on very large data volumes.

00:02:13.230 --> 00:02:17.104
And these built-in analytics capabilities support all major languages,

00:02:17.104 --> 00:02:19.652
including Python, R and Java.

00:02:20.370 --> 00:02:21.960
That brings us to speed.

00:02:22.470 --> 00:02:28.628
The Netezza Performance Server employs hardware components called Snippet Processing Units, or SPUs,

00:02:28.628 --> 00:02:31.341
which serve as the query processing engines.

00:02:31.560 --> 00:02:36.195
The hardware functions are further accelerated by the Field Programable Gate Arrays.

00:02:36.373 --> 00:02:43.101
FPGAs help the Netezza Performance Server provide deep analysis of petabytes of complex data with ease.

00:02:43.350 --> 00:02:47.159
With Netezza's unmatched speed comes best-in-class performance.

00:02:47.520 --> 00:02:49.300
Compared to its predecessor,

00:02:49.300 --> 00:02:53.484
the new Netezza Performance Server provides three times the SQL performance,

00:02:53.484 --> 00:02:55.043
two times the load performance,

00:02:55.043 --> 00:02:57.579
and two times the concurrency performance.

00:02:57.900 --> 00:03:02.530
All these speed improvements are powered by the NVME solid state drives,

00:03:02.530 --> 00:03:05.595
faster processors and a 64-bit code base.

00:03:05.730 --> 00:03:09.295
Translation: the cost of ownership is lower than ever before,

00:03:09.295 --> 00:03:14.134
yet you're getting increased ability and availability for critical Netezza workloads.

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:16.119
And perhaps best of all,

00:03:16.119 --> 00:03:20.079
upgrading from an existing Netezza appliance to the new Netezza Performance Server

00:03:20.079 --> 00:03:22.259
is risk free and couldn't be easier.

00:03:22.860 --> 00:03:26.394
Level up with a simple nzbackup and nzrestore,

00:03:26.394 --> 00:03:28.956
or with a single command nzmigrate.

00:03:29.433 --> 00:03:32.491
Netezza Performance Server built on Cloud Pak for Data System

00:03:32.491 --> 00:03:37.140
delivers unmatched power, simplicity, sophistication and speed.

00:03:37.450 --> 00:03:41.092
Whether you deploy in the cloud, hybrid, or on-premises,

00:03:41.092 --> 00:03:45.970
Netezza Performance Server is the essential data warehouse component in your journey to AI.

00:03:46.660 --> 00:03:48.745
Check out the links below to learn more.

